Campaign Forge: 5th Edition SRD 5.1 & 5.2 (fantasy d20) data pack
===================================================================

System Reference Document 5.1
-----------------------------

This work includes material taken from the System Reference Document 5.1 ("SRD 5.1") by Wizards of the Coast LLC and available at https://dnd.wizards.com/resources/systems-reference-document. The SRD 5.1 is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License available at https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode.

Changes made: the SRD 5.1 text and statistics were taken from the JSON
structuring of the SRD by 5e-bits/5e-database (below), reorganised into
Campaign Forge's data pack format: rule sections split into rule cards at
their headings, monster stat blocks mapped onto a character-sheet layout
(skill and save proficiencies stored as multipliers of the proficiency
bonus), dice tables in the text turned into roll tables, and a few source
errors corrected (see README.md, "Caveats"). Tables, generators, templates,
play advice, the calendar and the encounter terrain lists marked "Original"
are Campaign Forge's own and are not part of the SRD.

System Reference Document 5.2
-----------------------------

This work includes material from the System Reference Document 5.2 (“SRD 5.2”) by Wizards of the Coast LLC, available at https://www.dndbeyond.com/srd. The SRD 5.2 is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License, available at https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode.

Changes made: the SRD 5.2 backgrounds, species (with their lineages,
ancestries and legacies, and their traits), subclasses (with their
features) and feats were taken from the JSON structuring of the SRD 5.2 by
5e-bits/5e-database (below) and added to the module's character option
lists beside the SRD 5.1 ones, each marked with the edition label "2024"
and the source "SRD 5.2". Where an SRD 5.2 species, lineage, background or
subclass shares its name with an SRD 5.1 one, its name is followed by
"(2024)". Tables in the text were turned into Markdown tables, and two
source errors were corrected (see README.md, "Caveats").

This module is compatible with fifth edition rules. It is not affiliated
with, endorsed, sponsored or approved by Wizards of the Coast LLC.

